-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",382,{
[12193]="70033CA0\n1\tApproach the Grim and begin the battle.\tThe Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.\n2\tDefeat the Grim fueling the Easterlings furnace before it explodes\t This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12194]="70033CA1\n1\tDefeat the Grim fuelling the Easterlings' furnace\t This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12195]="7003181C\n1\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in northern Snowbourn. Gísling is frustrated by Fastred's distraction from the danger at hand, even with the disappearance of his son. He wants you to travel to Walstow with haste to aid Winsig and her people.\n2\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig can be found inside the Mead Hall of Walstow. The Orc-force has been repelled, and Walstow is safe for the moment. You should speak with Winsig in the aftermath of the battle.\n",
[12196]="70044314\n1\tSpeak with Dúneth\tDúneth can be found just outside Jal Kepir in Talath Anor. You should speak with Dúneth.\n2\tSpeak with Dúneth\tDúneth can be found in the hall of Crithost. You should speak with Dúneth.\n",
[12197]="7005B213\n1\tLure out and defeat Kaupur\tElta has offered to split the bounty for defeating Kaupur at Kordh Gúrat. Kordh Gúrat lies on the level below the middle tier, to the south-west of Aslíf.\n2\tTalk to Elta in Aslíf\tElta is waiting in Aslíf for your return with the \"armour.\"\n",
[12198]="70002D11\n1\tCollect Drake-egg\tAidan is waiting at Fail-á-Khro to the north-east of Aughaire. Lore-singer Arzhur has asked you to take the drake's egg to Aidan and then to fight by his side against the challengers from the clans loyal to Angmar.\n2\tSpeak with Aidan when you are ready to fight by his side.\tAidan is at Fail-á-Khro north-east of Aughaire. Fight alongside Aidan against the challengers from a hostile clan loyal to Angmar.\n3\tArzhur is at Aughaire, south-west of Fail-á-Khro. You should return to Arzhur and report of your victory against the first challenge.\t\n",
[12199]="700370F7\n1\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot in Marton in the northern Westfold. You should help Agelwyn choose one style of command for her first decision as acting Thane: 1. Should she make a decision herself and deliver the command to her people? 2. Should she ask her people to vote on what they think is best, and let the majority decide? 3. Should she listen to the people's opinions, and then make an informed decision? You must choose one.\t\n2\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot in Marton in the northern Westfold. You should speak with Agelwyn.\n",
[12200]="70000077\n1\tFind the first gear\tThe first missing gear is in a cave in the Winterheight, south-east of Thorin's Hall. Bávor has asked you to help reassemble the dwarf-built device which opens the Vault.\n2\tBring the gear to Bávor\030Collect Gear\tBávor is in Thorin's Hall. Bávor will be pleased to see you have acquired the first gear.\n",
[12201]="700572FD\n1\tInspect the illusion of the first stone\tAn illusion has appeared before you in the Crown Chamber. You should inspect the illusion of the first stone.\n2\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n3\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n4\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n5\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n6\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n7\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n8\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n9\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n10\tFind the first stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n11\tUnlock the door in the chamber\tThe clues have led you to a key. You should return to the chamber in the Grey Mountains and try it on the door.\n12\tRetrieve the first stone\tThe first stone is yours! You should retrieve it from the chamber in the Grey Mountains.\n13\tReturn the stone to its pedestal\tYou have found one of the missing stones! You should return it to its rightful place in the Crown Chamber.\n",
[12202]="70062DDF\n1\tExercise patience and learn Medwyn's secret\tMedwyn says he'll tell you the secret to successful fishing if you have patience. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Medwyn in Sedgemead\tMedwyn is pleased with your patience.\n",
[12203]="70062B14\n1\tTalk to Teilo Gwyniad\tTeilo Gwyniad is sitting on the pier in Lhan Garan. Teilo Gwyniad motioned for you to speak with him.\n2\tSalt a rack of fish (total: 5)\tThere are racks of drying fish on the pier in Lhan Garan. Teilo Gwyniad asked you to salt racks of fish on the pier.\n3\tTalk to Teilo Gwyniad\tYou have finished salting the fish as asked. Return to Madog on the pier in Lhan Garan.\n",
[12204]="700342AB\n1\tSpeak with the fishermen\tThe fisherman can likely be found at the lake's edge. You should search for the fisherman and encourage him to seek refuge in Forlaw.\n2\tSpeak with the fisherman\tThe two fishermen are at their camp on the edge of the Isingmere, in the northern Whitshaws. You should speak with the fishermen, now that they are done attacking you on sight.\n",
[12205]="7003528D\n1\tThe fishermen's supplies can be gathered around their camp in the north-eastern Whitshaws. You should gather the supplies.\t\n2\tBury supplies in adequate locations (total: 5)\tThe fishermen's home can be found south-west of their encampment on the lake. You should bring the supplies to the homestead and bury them, in hopes that they will be useful in the future.\n3\tReturn to Smala\tSmala can be found at the fishermen's encampment in the north-eastern Whitshaws. You should tell Smala that you have buried his supplies where he wished.\n",
[12206]="70034445\n1\tCollect fish from nets (total: 8)\tThe fish of today's catch can be found in nets along the northern edge of the Isingmere in the Whitshaws, near the fishermen's encampment. You should draw in the nets to gather fish for the two men's journey to Forlaw, for they will need fuel for their trek.\n2\tBring the fish to Smala\tThe fishermen can be found at the north-eastern edge of the Whitshaws on the edge of the Isingmere. You should bring the fish to the fishermen so that they will have food for their journey to Forlaw.\n",
[12207]="700342EC\n1\tDefeat harrying Warg-riders (total: 4)\030Defeat brutal Warg-riders (total: 2)\tHarrying Orcs riding on Wargs can be found in the northern Whitshaws. You should defeat several Orkish Warg-riders near the fishermen's haunt.\n2\tReturn to Morcar\tThe fishermen are at their small encampment on the banks of the Isingmere in the northern Whitshaws. You should speak with the fishermen.\n",
[12208]="70034AB6\n1\tCollect large cuts of moose-meat (total: 6)\tMoose can be found in the Whitshaws, especially towards the north. You should hunt moose and bring cuts of meat to the fishermen, so that they may bring it to Forlaw to help feed the people there.\n2\tBring the moose-meat to Morcar\tMorcar can be found at the fishermen's camp in the northern Whitshaws, on the edge of the Isingmere. You should bring the cuts of meat to Morcar.\n",
[12209]="70035A96\n1\tFind the fishermen's home\tGifemund spoke of two fishermen who live in a house in the Northern Whitshaws, near the edge of the lake and the woods. You should search for the fishermen's home.\n2\tExamine the fishing rack\tA fishing rack stands in front of the house in the northern Whitshaws. You should examine the fishing rack.\n",
[12210]="7001078F\n1\tCatch as many fish as you can in ten minutes\tThe pond is north of Bywater. Neddie Grub has invited you to fish from the Lithe Festival pond. All fish caught go back into the pond, but the more you catch, the more you win.\n",
[12211]="7000E8B8\n1\tDefeat Shataz\tThe troll Shataz was last seen by an Elvish scout on the slopes east of Orod Laden in the Misty Mountains, far to the south and east of the North Downs. Handarod has asked you to find the troll Shataz and defeat him.\n2\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the west and north of the Misty Mountains. You should return to Handarod and tell him of Shataz' defeat.\n",
[12212]="7004A393\n1\tDefeat Enforcers of Ugrukhôr (total: 12)\tDefeat Ugrukhôr's Enforcers you encounter in Udûn.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many of the Captain of the Pit's Enforcerers in Udûn.\n",
[12213]="70057610\n1\tFind the first missing stone\030Find the second missing stone\030Find the third missing stone\030Find the fourth missing stone\tTheir purpose remains unknown, but the path before you is clear. You must find the four missing stones.\n2\tReturn the Secret Stone to its pedestal\tOnly one stone remains. The Secret Stone. Do what you must.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin\tThe Shadowed King has been released from his prison. You must tell King Thorin what has happened!\n",
[12214]="7004A981\n1\tPurchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High-enchanters\tHigh-enchanters can be found in many camps around Gorgoroth, including the Udûn Foothold. Purchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High-enchanters.\n2\tTalk to Finnoth Sharp-wind\tFinnoth Sharp-wind can be found at the Udûn Foothold. You should talk to Finnoth Sharp-wind.\n3\tUse the Flame of Ancalamír to disenchant the Morgul-steel Dagger\tYou can purchase the Flame of Ancalamír from one of the High Enchanters. Use the Flame of Ancalamír to reduce the Morgul-steel Dagger to Motes of Enchantment.\n4\tTalk to Narthavron\tNarthavron can be found in the Udûn Foothold. You should talk to Narthavron.\n",
[12215]="7004B2DC\n1\tDefeat Lesser Fire Grims (total: 10)\tMornaur Furnaces can be found in Mornaur. You should attempt to douse the furnaces and defeat whatever lurks within.\n",
[12216]="70072EA4\n1\tBurn Ordâkhai tents (total: 5)\030Burn banners of Ordâkh (total: 8)\tYou have come to Onabóha to set the Ordâkhai tents and banners of Ordâkh on fire with the hope that the destruction will motivate them to move their camp elsewhere.\n2\tDefeat Potók Dólo\tYou have burned the enemy tents and banners at Onabóha and have drawn out their captain, Potók Dólo. You should defeat him.\n",
[12217]="700173C4\n1\tDefeat Ghâsh-hai Firebrands (total: 5)\030Defeat Ghâsh-hai Wrathcallers (total: 10)\tGhâsh-hai Orcs can be found within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch. Ossur sent you to face the Orc-forces of the fiery depths of Moria, who came to the Grand Stair to pay their tribute to Igash, an Orc devoted to Mazog.\n2\tTalk to Ossur at the Orc-watch\tOssur is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Ossur and inform him that you have defeated many of the Ghâsh-hai.\n",
[12218]="70040DF5\n1\tCollect Torthol's sheet music (total: 6)\tTorthol's sheet music is floating around the Court. You should pick up Torthol's sheet music.\n2\tReturn the sheet music to Torthol\tTorthol is in the Harper's Court in Dol Amroth. You should return the sheet music to Torthol.\n",
[12219]="7003FDE4\n1\tRestore statues (total: 11)\tThe statues are a symbol of Dol Amroth's ambitions for sea-faring.\n",
[12220]="70000016\n1\tBring the hops to Ponto Hopsbloom\030Collect hops (total: 12)\tFrog Hops grow in the marsh north of Frogmorton. The Floating Log Inn is in Frogmorton, south of the Frogmoors. Ponto Hopsbloom has asked you to pick some Frog Hops for his famous beer.\n",
[12221]="70041471\n1\tTalk to Glanion\030Talk to Durnir\tGlanion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Durnir can be found overlooking the Gilrain in Linhir. Garvir has asked you to speak to two of his captains, Glanion and Durnir, about the encroaching ruthless Dead and how Linhir might best defend itself.\n2\tTalk to Garvir\tGarvir can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Glanion and Durnir had but a few ideas of what can be done and seem demoralized. You should speak to Garvir.\n3\tTalk to Tancestel\tTancestel can be found near the river's edge in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Garvir has bid you speak to Tancestel, an old and superstitious man of Dor-en-Ernil, in the hope that he may have insight on these dire times.\n",
[12222]="7001A714\n1\tBring the goods to Watcher Rosecane\030Collect stolen-goods (total: 12)\tStolen goods are being kept by the brigands at Brigands' Watch. Watcher Rosecane requested that you search Brigands' Watch for goods stolen from the roadways and farms of Bree-land.\n",
[12223]="700037F8\n1\tTalk to Geitir\tGeitir is in Noglond, south on the road from Thorin's Halls. Tindr has asked you to speak with Geitir in Noglond to learn if the flow of water in the canal has returned to normal.\n",
[12224]="70070B02\n1\tDefeat Badharál the Gorger\030Defeat Maukhorn\030Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth\030Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent\tDefeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.\n",
})
